      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(auto-reply): handle stderr stream errors in sandbox media scpFile",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\n`scpFile` in `src/auto-reply/reply/stage-sandbox-media.ts` reads scp stderr for failure diagnostics but only attaches a `\"data\"` listener. If the stderr stream emits an `\"error\"` event during transfer or teardown, the error is unhandled and can crash the auto-reply staging flow.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nAdded an `\"error\"` listener to `child.stderr` that rejects the promise, and introduced a `settled` guard so the first error/exit outcome wins. This prevents double rejection and matches the stream-error handling pattern used elsewhere.\n\n## User Impact\n\nSandbox media staging via scp now fails gracefully with the stderr error instead of crashing on an unhandled stream error.\n\n## Evidence\n\nRegression test:\n\n```bash\npnpm test src/auto-reply/reply/stage-sandbox-media.scp.test.ts\n```\n\n```\nTest Files  1 passed (1)\n     Tests  1 passed (1)\n```\n\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\nReal process-level proof that a stderr stream error no longer crashes the auto-reply flow:\n\n```bash\nnode_modules/.bin/tsx scripts/proof/stage-sandbox-media-scp-stream-errors.mts\n```\n\n```\n=== Proof: stage-sandbox-media scpFile stderr stream error handling ===\n\nRejected with: stderr EPIPE\n\nPASS: stderr stream error was caught and scpFile rejected cleanly.\n```\n\n\n<!-- check-lint and check-test-types are green after fixing promise-executor lint in proof script. -->",
        "branch": "fix/stage-sandbox-media-scp-stream-errors",
